      "reviewInputFingerprint": "sha256:16c59aa76bcba411042cc652bdc5f840899160db244301d77a926fbb00a45c27",
      "descriptionVerdict": "KEEP",
      "descriptionRationale": "Reading and interpreting titration curves coherently links characteristic curve regions, equivalence and neutral conditions, buffering and indicator choice. It does not add an obligatory numerical pH-calculation competence simply because supporting cases provide computed data.",
      "positiveEvidenceMaterialVerdict": "KEEP",
      "positiveEvidenceMaterialRationale": "No remaining P blocker identified after reading all five whole current materials. Strong-acid and weak-acid tables, sharp endpoint neighbourhood and pKw-dependent neutral pH are consistent. Base cases distinguish strong and weak bases with different equivalence pH; the synthetic glycine two-stage table does not treat its first ampholyte point as a strong buffer. The actual image differentiates acid dissociation, acetate hydrolysis and OH excess. Case-specific calculation routes remain conditional, not a new universal quota.",
      "currentProfileStatusIsInputNotApproval": true
    },
