      "descriptionVerdict": "KEEP",
      "descriptionRationale": "The description explicitly requires actually performing a controlled Biuret investigation, evaluating positive and negative controls and explaining violet Cu(II) coordination to suitable peptide groups. These are connected aspects of one experiment competence.",
      "positiveEvidenceMaterialVerdict": "KEEP",
      "positiveEvidenceMaterialRationale": "No remaining P blocker identified. The complete bilingual SOP supplies teacher-authorized local risk assessment, measured quantities, fixed prevalidated CuSO4 dose, matched controls, real timed observations and cause-based repeat/postponement. Predictions or supplied reports do not prove actual performance. Blue free-amino-acid complexes and Cu(OH)2 precipitation are not violet peptide positives; Cu remains +II and disposal is local heavy-metal disposal, not a learner acidification recipe.",
      "currentProfileStatusIsInputNotApproval": true
    },
